IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 10: Referring to laws (ss 97 to 106A).
--
-- The chapter says what "law" means when an ACT law refers to another law (s 97),
-- how a reference to a law or a provision is read (ss 98, 99, 102 to 104, 106, 106A),
-- and the ways a law or provision may be referred to (ss 100, 101, 105).
-- The definitions printed inside s 97 and s 102 (5) are also in `act-section-definitions.l4`.
-- The rules below take the facts of the reference as plain inputs, because the text does not give a way to read a reference out of a document.
--
-- A rule that says a reference "may" be made in a way, or "includes" something, answers JUST TRUE when the facts match,
-- and NOTHING when they do not, because the text does not say that a reference made some other way, or to something else, is outside the rule.
-- A "means" definition answers TRUE or FALSE.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 10, Referring to laws`

§§ `Section 97: Definitions for the chapter`

-- The dictionary says what another jurisdiction is.
-- `somewhere else` is not in the text: it stands for any place the dictionary does not name.
-- src:3298 | another jurisdiction means the Commonwealth, a State, another Territory, the United Kingdom or New Zealand.
@ref dictionary, another jurisdiction (src:3298-3298)
DECLARE `Jurisdiction of a document` IS ONE OF
    `the Territory`
    `the Commonwealth`
    `a State`
    `another Territory`
    `the United Kingdom`
    `New Zealand`
    `somewhere else`

-- src:3298 | another jurisdiction means the Commonwealth, a State, another Territory, the United Kingdom or New Zealand.
@ref dictionary, another jurisdiction (the test) (src:3298-3298)
GIVEN jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction of a document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dictionary: the jurisdiction is another jurisdiction` MEANS
    CONSIDER jurisdiction
    WHEN `the Territory` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Commonwealth` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another Territory` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the United Kingdom` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `New Zealand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN FALSE

-- src:1380 | ACT law means an Act or statutory instrument.
-- src:1381 | Note A reference to an Act or statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of the Act or instrument (see s 7 and s 13).
@ref s 97 (1) (ACT law) (src:1380-1381)
GIVEN jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction of a document`, theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97 (1): the document is an ACT law` MEANS
    CONSIDER jurisdiction
    WHEN `the Territory` THEN theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrument
    WHEN `the Commonwealth` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a State` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another Territory` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the United Kingdom` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `New Zealand` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN FALSE

-- src:1383 | law of another jurisdiction means an Act or statutory instrument of another jurisdiction, and includes a provision of an Act or statutory instrument of another jurisdiction.
-- src:1384 | Note Another jurisdiction means the Commonwealth, a State, another Territory, the United Kingdom or New Zealand (see dict, pt 2).
@ref s 97 (1) (law of another jurisdiction) (src:1383-1384)
GIVEN jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction of a document`, theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN, theDocumentIsAProvisionOfAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97 (1): the document is a law of another jurisdiction` MEANS
    `dictionary: the jurisdiction is another jurisdiction` jurisdiction
    AND (theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction OR theDocumentIsAProvisionOfAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction)

-- src:1382 | law means an ACT law or a law of another jurisdiction.
@ref s 97 (1) (law) (src:1382-1382)
GIVEN jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction of a document`, theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN, theDocumentIsAProvisionOfAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97 (1): the document is a law` MEANS
    `s 97 (1): the document is an ACT law` jurisdiction theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction
    OR `s 97 (1): the document is a law of another jurisdiction` jurisdiction theDocumentIsAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction theDocumentIsAProvisionOfAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfThatJurisdiction

-- "Act, in relation to another Territory, includes ordinance."
-- src:1386 | Act, in relation to another Territory, includes ordinance.
@ref s 97 (2) (Act) (src:1386-1386)
GIVEN theDocumentIsAnOrdinanceOfTheOtherTerritory IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97 (2): the document is an Act in relation to the other Territory` MEANS
    IF   theDocumentIsAnOrdinanceOfTheOtherTerritory
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1387 | statutory instrument, of another jurisdiction, means an instrument (whether or not legislative in nature) made under—
-- src:1388 | (a) an Act of the other jurisdiction; or
-- src:1389 | (b) another statutory instrument of the other jurisdiction; or
-- src:1390 | (c) power given by an Act or statutory instrument of the other jurisdiction and also power given otherwise by law.
@ref s 97 (2) (statutory instrument of another jurisdiction) (src:1387-1390)
GIVEN theInstrumentIsMadeUnderAnActOfTheOtherJurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentIsMadeUnderAnotherStatutoryInstrumentOfTheOtherJurisdiction IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentIsMadeUnderPowerGivenByAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfTheOtherJurisdictionAndAlsoPowerGivenOtherwiseByLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97 (2): the instrument is a statutory instrument of another jurisdiction` MEANS
    theInstrumentIsMadeUnderAnActOfTheOtherJurisdiction
    OR theInstrumentIsMadeUnderAnotherStatutoryInstrumentOfTheOtherJurisdiction
    OR theInstrumentIsMadeUnderPowerGivenByAnActOrStatutoryInstrumentOfTheOtherJurisdictionAndAlsoPowerGivenOtherwiseByLaw

§§ `Section 98: References to ACT law include law containing reference`

-- "Of the same kind" is read as the same kind of Act or instrument as s 13 lists them.
-- src:1393 | In an ACT law, a reference in general terms to an ACT law of the same kind includes a reference to the law itself.
-- src:1394 | Example
-- src:1395 | The ABC Act 2001, s 27 gives a power to confiscate property under certain circumstances. Section 93 of the same Act provides ‘If an Act authorises the confiscation of property, the owner of the property has a right of appeal to the Magistrates Court.’ The right of appeal under s 93 also applies to the power given by s 27 because the reference to ‘an Act’ in s 93 includes a reference to the ABC Act 2001.
@ref s 98 (src:1393-1395)
GIVEN kindOfLawContainingTheReference IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`, kindOfLawReferredTo IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`, theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsInGeneralTerms IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98: the reference includes a reference to the law itself` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theReferenceIsInGeneralTerms AND (kindOfLawContainingTheReference EQUALS kindOfLawReferredTo)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 99: References in ACT statutory instruments to the Act`

-- src:1398 | In a statutory instrument, a reference to Act or the Act, without mentioning a particular Act, is a reference to the Act under which the instrument is made or in force.
@ref s 99 (src:1398-1398)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceMentionsNoParticularAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99: the reference is a reference to the Act under which the instrument is made or in force` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAStatutoryInstrument AND theReferenceMentionsNoParticularAct
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 100: Referring to particular ACT laws`

-- src:1401 | (1) An Act may be referred to by—
-- src:1402 | (a) the name the Act gives to itself; or
-- src:1403 | (b) the year it was passed and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to indicate that it is an Act.
@ref s 100 (1) (src:1401-1403)
DECLARE `Way of referring to an Act` IS ONE OF
    `by the name the Act gives to itself`
    `by the year the Act was passed and its number`
    `by some other way of naming an Act`

-- src:1401 | (1) An Act may be referred to by—
-- src:1402 | (a) the name the Act gives to itself; or
-- src:1403 | (b) the year it was passed and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to indicate that it is an Act.
@ref s 100 (1) (the rule) (src:1401-1403)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of referring to an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100 (1): an Act may be referred to in the way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `by the name the Act gives to itself` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `by the year the Act was passed and its number` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `by some other way of naming an Act` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1404 | (2) A statutory instrument may be referred to by—
-- src:1405 | (a) any name the instrument gives to itself; or
-- src:1406 | (b) if the instrument was notified in the register, the gazette or otherwise under section 61 (2) (b) and was numbered under this Act or another territory law—the year it was notified and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to the kind of instrument; or
-- src:1407 | (c) if the instrument was not notified but was numbered under a territory law—the year it was made and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to the kind of instrument; or
-- src:1408 | (d) if the instrument was notified in the gazette before the commencement of this Act—the number, date and page of the gazette where it was notified; or
-- src:1409 | (e) the date it was made, together with a reference to the Act or statutory instrument under which it was made.
@ref s 100 (2) (src:1404-1409)
DECLARE `Way of referring to a statutory instrument` IS ONE OF
    `by a name the instrument gives to itself`
    `by the year the instrument was notified and its number`
    `by the year the instrument was made and its number`
    `by the number, date and page of the gazette where the instrument was notified`
    `by the date the instrument was made and the law under which it was made`
    `by some other way of naming a statutory instrument`

-- (b) needs notification (in the register, the gazette or otherwise under s 61 (2) (b)) and numbering under this Act or another territory law;
-- (c) needs that the instrument was not notified but was numbered under a territory law;
-- (d) needs notification in the gazette before this Act commenced.
-- src:1404 | (2) A statutory instrument may be referred to by—
-- src:1405 | (a) any name the instrument gives to itself; or
-- src:1406 | (b) if the instrument was notified in the register, the gazette or otherwise under section 61 (2) (b) and was numbered under this Act or another territory law—the year it was notified and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to the kind of instrument; or
-- src:1407 | (c) if the instrument was not notified but was numbered under a territory law—the year it was made and its number, together with a reference (if necessary) to the kind of instrument; or
-- src:1408 | (d) if the instrument was notified in the gazette before the commencement of this Act—the number, date and page of the gazette where it was notified; or
-- src:1409 | (e) the date it was made, together with a reference to the Act or statutory instrument under which it was made.
@ref s 100 (2) (the rule) (src:1404-1409)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of referring to a statutory instrument`, theInstrumentWasNotified IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentWasNumberedUnderThisActOrAnotherTerritoryLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentWasNumberedUnderATerritoryLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentWasNotifiedInTheGazetteBeforeThisActCommenced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100 (2): a statutory instrument may be referred to in the way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `by a name the instrument gives to itself` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `by the year the instrument was notified and its number` THEN
        IF   theInstrumentWasNotified AND theInstrumentWasNumberedUnderThisActOrAnotherTerritoryLaw
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by the year the instrument was made and its number` THEN
        IF   (NOT theInstrumentWasNotified) AND theInstrumentWasNumberedUnderATerritoryLaw
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by the number, date and page of the gazette where the instrument was notified` THEN
        IF   theInstrumentWasNotifiedInTheGazetteBeforeThisActCommenced
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `by the date the instrument was made and the law under which it was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `by some other way of naming a statutory instrument` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Section 101: Referring to particular laws of other jurisdictions etc`

-- src:1412 | (1) In an ACT law, a law of another jurisdiction (the relevant law) may be referred to—
-- src:1413 | (a) by the name the relevant law gives to itself; or
-- src:1414 | (b) in any other way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the relevant law; or
-- src:1415 | (c) in any way that, under current legislative drafting practice, would be sufficient for referring to the relevant law if it were an ACT law;
-- src:1416 | together with a reference to the jurisdiction (or an abbreviation of the jurisdiction).
@ref s 101 (1) (src:1412-1416)
DECLARE `Way of referring to a law of another jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `by the name the other law gives to itself`
    `in a way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the law`
    `in a way that current legislative drafting practice would accept for an ACT law`
    `by some other way of naming a law of another jurisdiction`

-- src:1412 | (1) In an ACT law, a law of another jurisdiction (the relevant law) may be referred to—
-- src:1413 | (a) by the name the relevant law gives to itself; or
-- src:1414 | (b) in any other way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the relevant law; or
-- src:1415 | (c) in any way that, under current legislative drafting practice, would be sufficient for referring to the relevant law if it were an ACT law;
-- src:1416 | together with a reference to the jurisdiction (or an abbreviation of the jurisdiction).
@ref s 101 (1) (the rule) (src:1412-1416)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of referring to a law of another jurisdiction`, theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceAlsoNamesTheJurisdictionOrAnAbbreviation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101 (1): a law of another jurisdiction may be referred to in the way` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theReferenceAlsoNamesTheJurisdictionOrAnAbbreviation
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `by the name the other law gives to itself` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `in a way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the law` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `in a way that current legislative drafting practice would accept for an ACT law` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `by some other way of naming a law of another jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1417 | (2) In an ACT law, a provision of a law of another jurisdiction may be referred to—
-- src:1418 | (a) in a way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the provision; or
-- src:1419 | (b) in any way that, under current legislative drafting practice, would be sufficient for referring to the provision if it were a provision of an ACT law.
@ref s 101 (2) (src:1417-1419)
DECLARE `Way of referring to a provision of a law of another jurisdiction` IS ONE OF
    `in a way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the provision`
    `in a way that current legislative drafting practice would accept for a provision of an ACT law`
    `by some other way of naming a provision of a law of another jurisdiction`

-- src:1417 | (2) In an ACT law, a provision of a law of another jurisdiction may be referred to—
-- src:1418 | (a) in a way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the provision; or
-- src:1419 | (b) in any way that, under current legislative drafting practice, would be sufficient for referring to the provision if it were a provision of an ACT law.
@ref s 101 (2) (the rule) (src:1417-1419)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of referring to a provision of a law of another jurisdiction`, theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101 (2): a provision of a law of another jurisdiction may be referred to in the way` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `in a way sufficient in a law of the other jurisdiction for referring to the provision` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `in a way that current legislative drafting practice would accept for a provision of an ACT law` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `by some other way of naming a provision of a law of another jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1420 | (3) Subsection (2) does not limit any other provision of this chapter.
@ref s 101 (3) (src:1420-1420)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 101 (3): subsection (2) limits any other provision of this chapter` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Section 102: References to laws include references to laws as in force from time to time`

-- src:1423 | (1) In an ACT law, a reference to a law includes a reference to the following:
-- src:1424 | (a) the law as originally made, and as amended from time to time since it was originally made;
-- src:1425 | (b) if the law has been repealed and remade (with or without changes) since the reference was made—the law as remade (or last remade), and as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade);
-- src:1426 | (c) if a relevant provision of the law has been omitted and remade (with or without changes) in another law since the reference was made—the law in which the provision was remade (or last remade), as in force when the provision was remade (or last remade), and as amended from time to time since the provision was remade (or last remade).
@ref s 102 (1) (src:1423-1426)
DECLARE `Version of a law that a reference to the law may include` IS ONE OF
    `the law as originally made`
    `the law as amended from time to time since it was originally made`
    `the law as remade (or last remade)`
    `the law as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade)`
    `the law in which a relevant provision was remade (or last remade), as in force when the provision was remade`
    `the law in which a relevant provision was remade (or last remade), as amended from time to time since`

-- (b) needs that the law was repealed and remade since the reference was made;
-- (c) needs that a relevant provision was omitted and remade in another law since the reference was made.
-- src:1423 | (1) In an ACT law, a reference to a law includes a reference to the following:
-- src:1424 | (a) the law as originally made, and as amended from time to time since it was originally made;
-- src:1425 | (b) if the law has been repealed and remade (with or without changes) since the reference was made—the law as remade (or last remade), and as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade);
-- src:1426 | (c) if a relevant provision of the law has been omitted and remade (with or without changes) in another law since the reference was made—the law in which the provision was remade (or last remade), as in force when the provision was remade (or last remade), and as amended from time to time since the provision was remade (or last remade).
@ref s 102 (1) (the rule) (src:1423-1426)
GIVEN version IS A `Version of a law that a reference to the law may include`, theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theLawWasRepealedAndRemadeSinceTheReferenceWasMade IS A BOOLEAN, aRelevantProvisionWasOmittedAndRemadeInAnotherLawSinceTheReferenceWasMade IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102 (1): a reference to a law includes a reference to the version` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw
    THEN
        CONSIDER version
        WHEN `the law as originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the law as amended from time to time since it was originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the law as remade (or last remade)` THEN
            IF   theLawWasRepealedAndRemadeSinceTheReferenceWasMade
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `the law as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade)` THEN
            IF   theLawWasRepealedAndRemadeSinceTheReferenceWasMade
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `the law in which a relevant provision was remade (or last remade), as in force when the provision was remade` THEN
            IF   aRelevantProvisionWasOmittedAndRemadeInAnotherLawSinceTheReferenceWasMade
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `the law in which a relevant provision was remade (or last remade), as amended from time to time since` THEN
            IF   aRelevantProvisionWasOmittedAndRemadeInAnotherLawSinceTheReferenceWasMade
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1427 | (2) In an ACT law, a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the following:
-- src:1428 | (a) the provision as originally made, and as amended from time to time since it was originally made;
-- src:1429 | (b) if the provision has been omitted and remade (with or without changes and whether in the law or another law) since the reference was made—the provision as remade (or last remade), and as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade).
@ref s 102 (2) (src:1427-1429)
DECLARE `Version of a provision that a reference to the provision may include` IS ONE OF
    `the provision as originally made`
    `the provision as amended from time to time since it was originally made`
    `the provision as remade (or last remade)`
    `the provision as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade)`

-- (b) needs that the provision was omitted and remade, in the law or another law, since the reference was made.
-- src:1427 | (2) In an ACT law, a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the following:
-- src:1428 | (a) the provision as originally made, and as amended from time to time since it was originally made;
-- src:1429 | (b) if the provision has been omitted and remade (with or without changes and whether in the law or another law) since the reference was made—the provision as remade (or last remade), and as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade).
@ref s 102 (2) (the rule) (src:1427-1429)
GIVEN version IS A `Version of a provision that a reference to the provision may include`, theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theProvisionWasOmittedAndRemadeSinceTheReferenceWasMade IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102 (2): a reference to a provision of a law includes a reference to the version` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw
    THEN
        CONSIDER version
        WHEN `the provision as originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the provision as amended from time to time since it was originally made` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the provision as remade (or last remade)` THEN
            IF   theProvisionWasOmittedAndRemadeSinceTheReferenceWasMade
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `the provision as amended from time to time since it was remade (or last remade)` THEN
            IF   theProvisionWasOmittedAndRemadeSinceTheReferenceWasMade
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1430 | (3) To remove any doubt, if the name of a law is amended, a reference in an ACT law to the law by its name before the amendment includes a reference to the law by its name as amended.
@ref s 102 (3) (src:1430-1430)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theNameOfTheLawHasBeenAmended IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceUsesTheNameBeforeTheAmendment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102 (3): the reference includes a reference to the law by its name as amended` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theNameOfTheLawHasBeenAmended AND theReferenceUsesTheNameBeforeTheAmendment
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 47 is outside this encoding's scope; the sections a rule is subject to are listed, as s 73 (5) does in the commencement module.
-- src:1431 | (4) This section is subject to section 47 (Statutory instrument may make provision by applying law or instrument).
@ref s 102 (4) (src:1431-1431)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 102 (4): the sections that s 102 is subject to` MEANS LIST "47"

§§ `Section 103: References to repealed laws`

-- src:1436 | In an ACT law, a reference to a law as repealed is a reference to the law as in force immediately before it was repealed.
@ref s 103 (src:1436-1436)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsToTheLawAsRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 103: the reference is a reference to the law as in force immediately before it was repealed` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theReferenceIsToTheLawAsRepealed
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 104: References to laws include references to instruments under laws`

-- src:1439 | (1) In an ACT law, a reference (either generally or specifically) to a law includes a reference to the statutory instruments made or in force under the law.
@ref s 104 (1) (src:1439-1439)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsToALaw IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentIsMadeOrInForceUnderTheLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104 (1): the reference includes a reference to the statutory instrument` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theReferenceIsToALaw AND theInstrumentIsMadeOrInForceUnderTheLaw
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1440 | (2) In subsection (1), a reference to the statutory instruments made or in force under the law includes a reference to any law or instrument applied, adopted or incorporated (with or without change) under the law.
@ref s 104 (2) (src:1440-1440)
GIVEN theLawOrInstrumentIsAppliedAdoptedOrIncorporatedUnderTheLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104 (2): the reference to the statutory instruments made or in force under the law includes a reference to the law or instrument` MEANS
    IF   theLawOrInstrumentIsAppliedAdoptedOrIncorporatedUnderTheLaw
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1441 | (3) This chapter applies to an instrument applied, adopted or incorporated under a law as if—
-- src:1442 | (a) the instrument were a law; and
-- src:1443 | (b) any other necessary changes were made.
@ref s 104 (3) (src:1441-1443)
GIVEN theInstrumentIsAppliedAdoptedOrIncorporatedUnderALaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104 (3): this chapter applies to the instrument as if it were a law, with any other necessary changes made` MEANS
    IF   theInstrumentIsAppliedAdoptedOrIncorporatedUnderALaw
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 105: Referring to provisions of laws`

-- src:1446 | In an ACT law, a provision of a law may be referred to by reference to the provision of the law in which it is contained.
-- src:1447 | Example
-- src:1448 | Paragraph (b) of subsection (2) of section 10 of an Act may be referred to by reference to the section, subsection and paragraph, that is, as section 10 (2) (b).
@ref s 105 (src:1446-1448)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsByReferenceToTheProvisionOfTheLawInWhichTheProvisionIsContained IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105: the provision of the law may be referred to in the way` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theReferenceIsByReferenceToTheProvisionOfTheLawInWhichTheProvisionIsContained
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 106: References to provisions of laws are inclusive`

-- The position is where the provision stands in the law, counting along the law from the start;
-- a heading between two sections takes a position between theirs (the second example).
-- A provision outside the beginning, the end and what lies between is not within the reference.
-- src:1451 | In an ACT law, a reference to any part of a law is a reference to the following:
-- src:1452 | (a) the provision of the law that begins the part;
-- src:1453 | (b) the provision of the law that ends the part;
-- src:1454 | (c) any provision of the law between the beginning and end of the part.
-- src:1455 | Examples
-- src:1456 | 1 A reference to ‘sections 5 to 9’ includes both section 5 and section 9.
-- src:1457 | 2 A reference to ‘sections 260 to 264’ includes a provision such as a part heading between section 260 and section 261.
-- src:1458 | 3 A reference to ‘from child to adult’ includes both the word ‘child’ and the word ‘adult’.
@ref s 106 (src:1451-1458)
GIVEN position IS A NUMBER, positionOfTheProvisionThatBeginsThePart IS A NUMBER, positionOfTheProvisionThatEndsThePart IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106: the provision is within a reference to the part of the law` MEANS
    IF   position EQUALS positionOfTheProvisionThatBeginsThePart
         OR position EQUALS positionOfTheProvisionThatEndsThePart
         OR (position GREATER THAN positionOfTheProvisionThatBeginsThePart AND position LESS THAN positionOfTheProvisionThatEndsThePart)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Section 106A: References to paragraphs etc of laws`

-- src:1461 | (1) In an ACT law, a reference to a paragraph of a provision of a law includes any words in the provision before or after the paragraph that are necessary or desirable to make the reference meaningful.
-- src:1462 | Note Although this section contains a reference to an ACT law and a reference to a law, s 98 makes it clear that the references can be to the same law.
@ref s 106A (1) (src:1461-1462)
GIVEN theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsToAParagraphOfAProvisionOfALaw IS A BOOLEAN, theWordsAreInTheProvisionBeforeOrAfterTheParagraph IS A BOOLEAN, theWordsAreNecessaryOrDesirableToMakeTheReferenceMeaningful IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106A (1): the reference includes the words` MEANS
    IF   theReferenceIsInAnACTLaw AND theReferenceIsToAParagraphOfAProvisionOfALaw AND theWordsAreInTheProvisionBeforeOrAfterTheParagraph AND theWordsAreNecessaryOrDesirableToMakeTheReferenceMeaningful
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
